 One entry for every build handed to a person (a kept build, a desktop build, a test build), newest on top. `node tools/version.mjs --next` adds the entry and raises the build counter in `tools/version.json` together, in the commit that is built. Each entry has two parts: **For players** in plain words, which Orb reads before it is used anywhere (no team nicknames, what a player presses and sees), and **For the team**, the commit subjects since the last entry. Build 0 means no build has been numbered yet.
 
+## 0.1.1 (2026-11-23, 66d4e460)
+
+For players
+This is the first numbered build. What is new to hold in your hands:
+- The game starts on a list of modes. Pick one with the pad, pick your fighter with the d-pad, and start.
+- Press Start in a match and a pause menu opens. Its Quit row asks "Close the game?" with Stay lit, so a slip of the thumb does not close anything; choose "Close the game" and it closes.
+- The computer fighters on Easy and Medium now answer a move you hold: a charge you keep holding is answered by a grab or a step out of the way, so holding a button down no longer wins by itself.
+Not in this entry on purpose: the planet sizes (small, medium and big) are still being finished.
+
+For the team
+- Game Design: gauntlet plan records X-06's bands and final read, and rules that the idle training dummy skips the hold answer
+- Legal: gate G11's proof now on the round planet (1,799 people, none died); RL-230 holds with the 8-slot listener
+- Netcode: the ENet listener keeps spare slots so a dropped call can't block the live one (the late-host race); the check makes the key before listen, with a stall row and its one-slot control in CI
+- Rendering: steady-fill collapse attribution (medium passes; small and tiny fail on two Rendering bugs, the marks' slope and bowl rims in the foreground line)
+- Netcode: ENet check prints both peers' errors and a caller's retry state (diagnostics only, for the late-host timeout)
+- Encounter: X-06 side effects read (no hold-answer bug; Medium pace matching explains the scene shifts; match length unchanged within noise)
+- Tools: hold_answer_check wired into CI; four flash scenes re-staged longer for X-06 (no guard loosened), scenes-2 split in two
